{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The driver was physically at the pickup when the arrival event fired. The platform trip record puts auto-arrival from driver GPS at 13:27:15 on 2026-09-17 at Block 216, Serangoon Avenue 4, and the GPS trace corroborates it: the nearest fix (index 12, 13:27:10) sits 0.497 m from the pickup point with a reported horizontal accuracy of 6 m, well inside the 50 m arrival radius that applies to a STANDARD pickup zone, and the trace reports accuracy on every fix so the 25 m accuracy filter is satisfied, not evaded. The arrival test under POL-NS-21 is therefore met on the platform's own evidence, at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05069", "EV-GPS-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21"],
      "relies_on": "gps_trace.derived.v7.arrival_check.corroborated",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The free wait ran in full before the driver cancelled. Arrival at 13:27:15 starts the 300 s clock under POL-NS-21, so the free wait ended at 13:32:15; the platform logged 'free wait period expired; rider not on board' at 13:32:20 and the driver cancelled at 13:33:40, 385 s after arrival and 85 s after the wait expired. The trace shows the vehicle stationary at the pickup from 13:27:10 to 13:33:40 (speed 0 kph on every fix in that span), so the driver did not merely touch and go; he waited out the free period before cancelling. POL-NS-21 is satisfied and POL-NS-22's precondition - a driver cancellation after the free wait - is met.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05069", "EV-GPS-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-21", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.free_wait.seconds_from_start_to_cancel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver discharged the POL-NS-23 contact obligation in both limbs, before cancelling. He sent in-app chat messages at 13:27:40 (MSG-05069-001, 'Hi I'm at Blk 216 drop off') and 13:32:00 (MSG-05069-003, 'Hello?'), and he placed an in-app call at 13:30:15 (MSG-05069-002, channel VOICE_CALL_LOG, 'Outgoing in-app call to rider - not answered (rang 24 s)'). All three entries pre-date trip_record.cancelled_at of 13:33:40. POL-NS-23 expressly accepts 'a voice-call entry in the chat log' as the call limb, and the platform chat log is a COMPLETE artifact at weight 1.0 whose derived contact check records complete = true, call_count = 1 and obligation_met = true. The clause is satisfied and the fee is not voided.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05069", "EV-TRIP-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.derived.v7.contact_before_cancel.obligation_met",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's counter-statement - 'He never called me, he only sent messages' - is contradicted by the platform's own voice-call record and does not defeat the contact obligation. POL-NS-23 requires that the driver place at least one in-app call, not that the rider answer it; the log records an outgoing call placed at 13:30:15 that rang for 24 s unanswered, which is precisely the situation the clause contemplates. The rider may not have registered the call, but the obligation is judged on the placed call, and the placed call is on the record at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-05069", "EV-TRIP-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-23"],
      "relies_on": "chat_log.messages[1].channel",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-24 does not assist the rider here. That clause gives a rider a free cancellation only where the driver fails to arrive by the scheduled pickup time plus 5 minutes and the rider then cancels; this trip was on-demand, it was cancelled by the driver and not by the rider, and the driver in fact arrived at 13:27:15. Nor can the 5.00 SGD goodwill credit under POL-NS-24 arise, because it is conditioned on a failure to attempt contact and the chat log records an attempted call as well as two messages. There is no driver no-show on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05069", "EV-CHAT-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-24"],
      "relies_on": "trip_record.cancelled_by",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The fee was correctly charged at the policy figure and belongs to the driver. The payments ledger records a 5.00 SGD cancellation fee, category NO_SHOW_CHARGE, with fee_matches_policy = true against the POL-NS-22 schedule of 5.00 SGD, and POL-NS-22 directs that a fee charged after a post-free-wait cancellation is transferred to the driver as compensation for time and fuel. On the merits the driver is owed that 5.00 SGD, and under POL-GEN-03 the ruling is DRIVER_COMPENSATION with amount_sgd and driver_compensation_sgd both 5.00.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-05069", "EV-TRIP-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-22", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.derived.money.driver_compensation_if_upheld_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "NO_ACTION would be the wrong outcome and would simply entrench the error. The interim reversal at 13:25:40 (recorded as fee_reversed) refunded the 5.00 SGD to the rider and withheld it from the driver, pending this review. POL-GEN-03 makes NO_ACTION party-relative: it means the filing party's claim is not supported and the present state stands. Here the driver's claim IS supported - the free wait was served and the contact obligation was met - so leaving the present state standing would leave the driver 5.00 SGD out of pocket on a fee the policy awards him. The driver asks for DRIVER_COMPENSATION of 5.00 SGD, not for a further or separate payment.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05069", "EV-FARE-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-22"],
      "relies_on": "fare_breakdown.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing in this record requires escalation. The two facts the no-show rules turn on - when the driver arrived, and whether he messaged and called before cancelling - are both established by COMPLETE artifacts at weight 1.0 (the platform trip record, the GPS trace and the chat log), so POL-GEN-26's condition, a fact the evidence cannot establish, is not met. The contested value is 5.00 SGD, below POL-GEN-22's 10.00 SGD band, so the AI ruling is final at any confidence; neither profile carries a fraud flag, so no 0.95 bar applies; and POL-NS-26 makes the AI ruling final on a 5.00 SGD no-show, subject only to POL-GEN-21, which is not engaged because no safety indicator appears anywhere on this record.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-05069", "EV-GPS-05069", "EV-CHAT-05069"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-26", "POL-GEN-22", "POL-NS-26"],
      "relies_on": "dispute.amount_contested_sgd",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
